# title: Up-and-out call
# category: Barriers and touch options
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: An at-the-money call that dies if the stock ever closes at or above 130% of its initial level.
#
# Barrier: 130% of the strike-date level, checked at every close (a daily
# grid approximates continuous monitoring). No rebate.

2027-01-04
    s0 = spot()
    alive = 1

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() >= 1.30 * s0 then alive = 0 endIf

2028-01-04
    if spot() >= 1.30 * s0 then alive = 0 endIf
    if alive = 1 then pays max(spot() - s0, 0) endIf
